  v_ref := public.authored_item_register(p_ref => $vf$authored:inf-ind-2$vf$, p_task => $vf$r.inference$vf$, p_task_key => $vf$authored-inference$vf$, p_role_class => $vf$assessment$vf$, p_intended_role => $vf$independent_check$vf$, p_group => $vf$inf-i2$vf$, p_body => $vf${"format":"choice_evidence","sentences":["Small towns that lose their only grocery store rarely notice the full cost at once.","Residents simply drive to the next town, and life seems to go on.","Over time, however, the trip becomes a reason to shop, eat, and see a doctor elsewhere as well.","The pharmacy and the café that depended on grocery shoppers begin to close one by one.","The store, it turns out, was not one thread in the town's fabric but the knot that held many threads together.","When planners decide which businesses to support, they should ask what else depends on them."],"stem":"밑줄 친 \"the knot that held many threads together\"가 다음 글에서 의미하는 바로 가장 적절한 것은?","choices":["a shop that relied on nearby businesses for its customers","a store that sold enough goods to spare residents a trip","a business that competed with the pharmacy and the café","the shop that brought the most money into the town","a business whose loss drags other local life down too"]}$vf$::jsonb, p_gold => $vf${"answer":4,"decisive":3,"evidence":[2,3],"evidenceAlt":[4,5],"rationale":"식료품점이 사라지자 사람들이 다른 볼일도 밖에서 보게 되고 약국·카페가 차례로 문을 닫았다 — 이 가게가 다른 지역 활동들을 붙잡아 두던 중심이었다는 뜻이다(4번).","distractors":[{"choice":0,"design":"reversed","why":"의존의 방향을 뒤집었다 — 약국·카페가 식료품점 손님에 기댔다(4번)."},{"choice":1,"design":"distorted","why":"'여러 실'을 한 가게의 여러 상품으로 글자 그대로 읽었다 — 글의 실은 다른 가게·활동이다."},{"choice":2,"design":"reversed","why":"약국·카페는 경쟁자가 아니라 식료품점 덕에 살던 가게다(4번)."},{"choice":3,"design":"off_text","why":"수익 규모는 글에 나오지 않는다."}]}$vf$::jsonb, p_annotation_ref => $vf$authored-inference-inf-ind-2.v1$vf$, p_provenance => $vf${"author":"Claude (Claude Code agent, Vocaflow FINAL session)","method":"Vocaflow 자체 창작 — 기출 지문을 옮기거나 고쳐 쓰지 않았다","derivedFrom":[],"c