8bc2379a506a","prompt_sha256":"0eae8d6239b8cca04ba79c0046506def6c12903c6c90e4bf9356dcafcf2e3058","response_sha256":"e47d588985970049734477e32412d46b02ccd4d3286a1d89e0894e930f6432bb","source_file_sha256":"2763dfa3786da48773b54f0f74e3eb8dcf0ceeb710924d478aefe94c59995358","verdict":"accept","items":[{"id":"sem-guided-1","verdict":"accept","gold_issues":[],"why":"In sentence 2 (0-based), 'Among them' refers back to the old tools in sentence 1, so the hammer is one of the tools. Expression a (hammer) is the narrower term inside b (tools), so 'hyponym' with same=false is correct. Both hints use 1-based sentence numbers, matching proseNumbering, and they point to the right sentences. The Korean is accurate."},{"id":"sem-ind-2","verdict":"accept","gold_issues":[],"why":"'far from hasty' negates 'hasty', which gives 'deliberate/careful'. In context, spending two weeks studying every report and the slow, careful plan in sentence 4 show both expressions describe the same behaviour, so 'paraphrase' with same=true is defensible. A strict reader could note that 'far from hasty' does not on its own entail 'slow'. That is a nuance, not a defect, because the passage supports the slowness. The why text uses 1-based numbers correctly (5번 = index 4)."},{"id":"sem-transfer-1","verdict":"accept","gold_issues":[],"why":"'let students choose their own reading books' (sentence 0) and 'Being free to decide what to read' (sentence 3) describe the same policy with a different subject and structure, so this is a phrase-level paraphrase with same=true. The prose references (1번, 4번) are correct, and the English is natural."},{"id":"sem-ind-4","verdict":"accept","gold_issues":[],"why":"'prompt' sums up being served almost at once (sentence 1). 'sluggish' sums up the twenty-minute waits (sentence 2). They are opposite ends of the same scale, service speed, so 'antonym' with same=false is correct. The why text's prose references (2번, 3번) map correctly to indexes 1 and 2."},{"id":"sem-transfer-2","verdict":"accept","gold_issues":[],"why":"Wednesday is one of the weekdays, and the weekday/weekend frame is set by sentences 0 and 1. Expression a is included in b, so 'hyponym' with same=false is correct. The why text's prose references (1번 평일, 2번 주말) are correct, and the Korean is accurate."}]},{"agent":"codex","session_id":"01a16728-fc3c-7bd0-a9ec-7031e5c2035b","request_id":"429e2f99-7098-446d-a7de-7ffc90ad348c","prompt_sha256":"0eae8d6239b8cca04ba79c0046506def6c12903c6c90e4bf9356dcafcf2e3058","response_sha256":"0835c512ca2bac7f609c60daff9715566780f3914e625f28ff5707bea43b9a9c","source_file_sha256":"2763dfa3786da48773b54f0f74e3eb8dcf0ceeb710924d478aefe94c59995358","verdict":"accept","items":[{"id":"sem-guided-1","verdict":"accept","gold_issues":[],"why":"hammer는 tools의 하위어이므로 same=false와 hyponym이 타당하다. 문장 인덱스와 표시 표현이 정확하며, 두 힌트와 한국어 해설도 관계의 방향을 올바르게 설명한다."},{"id":"sem-ind-2","verdict":"accept","gold_issues":[],"why":"두 주 동안 보고서를 검토했다는 문맥에서 far from hasty는 slow and careful과 같은 신중한 접근을 나타낸다. 문맥상 same=true와 paraphrase가 타당하다. 한국어 해설의 부정 해석도 맞으며, 이 판단은 두 표현의 보편적 논리적 동치가 아닌 해당 문맥에 근거한다."},{"id":"sem-transfer-1","verdict":"accept","gold_issues":[],"why":"두 표현은 학생에게 읽을 책을 선택할 자유를 주는 동일한 제도를 학교와 학생의 관점에서 각각 기술한다. same=true와 paraphrase가 타당하며, 해설은 지문 밖의 연구 결과를 주장하지 않는다."},{"id":"sem-ind-4","verdict":"accept","gold_issues":[],"why":"즉시 응대하는 첫 카페와 주문 처리가 지연되는 둘째 카페의 대조가 prompt와 sluggish의 반대 의미를 명확히 뒷받침한다. same=false와 antonym, 문장 인덱스 및 한국어 해설이 모두 타당하다."},{"id":"sem-transfer-2","verdict":"accept","gold_issues":[],"why":"Wednesday는 weekdays에 포함되는 특정 요일이므로 A에서 B로의 관계는 hyponym이다. same=false, 표시 위치, 근거 문장 및 한국어 해설이 일치한다."}]}],"judgment":"accepted_candidate_content_and_gold","rights_basis":"first_party_original_declaration_only","rights_grant":false,"human_review_claimed":false,"not_reviewed":["sem-teach-1","sem-ind-1","sem-delayed-1","sem-ind-3"]}$vf$::jsonb; v_ref text; v_decision uuid;
